### Variables
# Set WEBHOOK_SECRET to match your .env value
# The signatures below were computed with secret = "dev-secret-changeme"
# Recompute: printf '%s' '<compact-json>' | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "dev-secret-changeme"
#
# Deduplication is based on SHA-256 hash of the request body.
# Sending the same body twice returns 200 + duplicate:true.

### Local — Normal webhook (202 + background processing, full context)
POST http://localhost:8080/webhook/github
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=1c433d1a7e7a6b4349bbe00438cc89b292e9d4b09adce66f313bbd4ab491f71f

{"repo":"gugacarbo/user-request-issue-writter","requester":{"name":"Alice","email":"alice@example.com"},"payload":{"descricao":"The login button is broken. When I click it, nothing happens.","url_atual":"https://app.example.com/login","categoria":"bug","contexto_da_sessao":"Chrome 120 on macOS","logs_do_console":"TypeError: cannot read addEventListener","logs_de_rede":"POST /api/login 500"}}

### Local — Duplicate body (same body as above → 200 duplicate:true)
